 34SI c  2010Ze03: a 100-MeV/nucleon {+34}P secondary beam was produced via     
 34SI2c  fragmentation of a {+40}Ar primary beam from the NSCL CCF impinging on 
 34SI3c  a 611-mg/cm2 Be target, separated by the A1900 fragment separator, and 
 34SI4c  impinged on a 2.6 mg/cm2 natLi (92.4% 7Li) target. |g rays were        
 34SI5c  detected by SeGA array of fifteen 32-fold segmented Ge detectors. 34Si 
 34SI6c  nuclei were identified and momentum analyzed by the S800 spectrograph. 
 34SI7c  Measured E|g with Doppler correction, I|g, ({+34}Si)|g-coin, and       
 34SI8c  ({+34}Si)({+7}Be) coin. Deduced Gamow-Teller strength distributions.   
 34SI9c  Comparisons with shell-model calculations.                              
